module

public import MathlibExt.NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction.BiunitaryTriperfect

/-!
# Biunitary triperfect numbers with exact exponent four at two

The biunitary triperfect numbers with exact exponent four at two and exponent three or four
at three equal `2160`. The theorem `eq_2160_of_factorization_two_eq_four` is proved in
`MathlibExt.NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction.BiunitaryTriperfect`, next to the biunitary
divisor-sum lemmas it uses; this module re-exports it.

Source: Tomohiro Yamada, *Determining all Biunitary Triperfect Numbers of a Certain Form*,
Journal of Integer Sequences 28 (2025), Article 25.4.5, Lemma 14.
-/
